  "passFactRules": "A leg recorded as passed must carry EVERY key of legFacts[leg] and satisfy every rule in passFacts[leg]; keys without a rule are recorded but unconstrained. A rule is a literal (strict equality; booleans and integers are never coerced), {\"not\": v} (differs from v and has the type of v), {\"min\": n} (integer >= n), {\"type\": \"boolean\"} (must be true or false, never null), or {\"equalsFact\": key} (equals another fact of the same leg). failed and skipped legs are unconstrained. A table naming an unknown leg or fact, an unrecognised rule form, a type-mismatched literal, or an equalsFact across types is a contract error, never ignored.",
